# Pi as npm publishes it. janis-install installs @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent
# and the packages it depends on, as package-lock.json pins them, from a copy of
# their registry files the site serves (prepare-pi-npm.mjs). The pi command runs
# dist/cli.js in its own process; npm's bin, dist/bundle/cli.js, would need
# Node's require of ES modules and runs the undici it bundles.
FROM /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-system 03f140fb3ed97157f3f45f3626724bce234733e0493058bac068d9b7f093b112
INSTALL /v0.1.4/demos/javascript/Dollyfile-janis-install 23d6d65323aff44276238f387b3df13165e6f5313719b429773722c68292b339
INSTALL /v0.1.4/demos/rust/Dollyfile-ripgrep 50b315502450edf05496cf43f5f0ffe0d924b35c29ba8ff1a7ebb8bba853e015
INSTALL /v0.1.4/demos/rust/Dollyfile-fd 3a248527e6b1aeac1303d34a8dfe78bc6dfe2a243ac8085074549ba81d215aa0
REQUIRES HEADER quickjs-runner
REQUIRES LIB    dolly-js
REQUIRES LIB    quickjs
REQUIRES TOOL   cc
REQUIRES TOOL   find
REQUIRES TOOL   janis-install
REQUIRES TOOL   rm
REQUIRES TOOL   tar

SOURCE /v0.1.4/dist/static/default/pi-npm.tar     6ebb57dbb6755bce129249e8e3c5cad349139979a4a8aff6c9520a8e16650c1f /tmp/pi-npm.tar
SOURCE /v0.1.4/dist/static/default/commands/pi.c  2296ec09e6b95b0d0dd065f806138e48eaad855d77d6366adfdfc33d720da98e /tmp/pi.c
SLOP tar -xf /tmp/pi-npm.tar -C /
SLOP janis-install --registry /tmp/pi-npm @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent@1.0.3
# Pi is an application nothing compiles against: its tree's source maps and
# type declarations, 50 MB of its 111, go.
SLOP find /usr/lib/node_modules -type f \( -name '*.map' -o -name '*.d.ts' -o -name '*.d.mts' -o -name '*.d.cts' \) -exec rm {} +
SLOP cc -I /usr/include/dolly /tmp/pi.c -ldolly-js -lquickjs -o /usr/bin/pi
SLOP rm -rf /tmp/pi-npm /tmp/pi-npm.tar /tmp/pi.c
FOLDER /usr/lib/node_modules

EXPORTS ENV PI_PACKAGE_DIR /usr/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent
EXPORTS ENV PI_SKIP_VERSION_CHECK 1
EXPORTS TOOL pi

SLOP pi --version
FILE /usr/share/man/cat1/pi.1
    pi: the Pi coding agent as npm publishes it, running under QuickJS-ng and
    Janis, with the janis-install, ripgrep and fd packages.
    
      pi                 starts the agent; /exit or Ctrl+D leaves it
      pi --offline       no network at startup; model requests still go out
    
    The pi-dolly package adds Dolly's prompt, skill, settings and theme; with
    it the bash tool and ! run Slop, and a download tool hands a file to the page.
    Requests go through the page's HTTP broker and its policy; OAuth logins
    depend on the provider's CORS, and there is no callback listener.
    Conversations are in ~/.pi/agent/sessions (pi --resume), credentials in
    ~/.pi/agent/auth.json: a saved session keeps them. There is no npm client:
    Pi packages that need npm or native addons fail to install;
    dependency-free JavaScript extensions go in ~/.pi/agent/extensions/.
